    "scribes-003": {
      "date": "2026-11-17",
      "decision": "applied_with_word_withheld",
      "normalized_latin": "tremet [intinctus?] iterum calamus",
      "reason": "The verb tremet and the nominative calamus support a trembling pen. The word divided at the line ending is iterum. The sequence before it appears to read intinctus, a masculine participle that can describe a dipped pen. The earlier reading intuitus gave “my sight” more certainty than the type warrants. The brackets in the English mark the unresolved modifier. A Latin reader should adjudicate the letterforms, the syntax and the placement of iterum.",
